# Review

This plugin provides two skills for review workflows.

## multi-agent-review

Orchestrate a structured review using independent specialist agents. Use when
the review target benefits from multiple dimensions or specialist perspectives;
do not use for a simple single-perspective review.

**Frame the review** — establish context, scope, review dimensions (correctness,
security, performance, maintainability, accessibility, operational safety), and
review policy before dispatching agents.

**Dispatch independent reviewers** — assign each reviewer an explicit subset of
the scope and one or more dimensions. Use independent agents in parallel. Give
every reviewer the same context, scope, dimensions, review policy, and the
reviewer-result schema.

**Triage and consolidate** — drop findings with confidence below 80, group by
underlying problem, merge findings that describe the same issue, and retain
unresolved conflicts as conflict sets.

**Validate** — send every finding to a validation agent that did not author it.
Only present verified findings in the final result.

**Present** — start with scope, dimensions, and outcome. Show findings in
priority order (verified first, then needs-attention, then unresolved conflicts).
Assign user-facing IDs (`R-01`, `R-02`, …) after consolidation.

## pr-review-comments

Format review findings as GitHub pull request review comments. Place each
comment at the precise file path and line range it addresses. Use the diff
context to anchor comments accurately. Group related comments when they address
the same underlying issue.
